# Oracle checker evidence · `guide:docgen:oracle-evidence`

The public bounded reader validates one closed payload and preserves typed exact-arithmetic resource faults. Its tests consume the same small CC0 fixture as documentation checking.

**Table (Oracle controls)** · `tab:docgen:oracle-controls`

|Test|Claim|
|----|-----|
|(`test:unit:oracle-admits-sample-evidence`)|All five kinds and the original route intersections are admitted.|
|(`test:unit:oracle-refuses-evidence-mutations`)|Disagreement, changed publication, missing, duplicate, stray and swapped evidence, and unknown routes are refused.|
|(`test:unit:oracle-refuses-malformed-forms`)|Envelope, operation, target, refusal, rational and ordering failures retain typed causes.|
|(`test:unit:oracle-checks-exact-results-and-width`)|Promised exact results and the inclusive width ceiling are enforced.|
|(`test:unit:oracle-enforces-resource-boundaries`)|Exact-limit and one-below capacities and prior consumption are checked.|
|(`test:unit:oracle-refuses-json-ambiguity`)|Duplicate keys, trailing input and excessive nesting cannot overwrite evidence.|
|(`test:unit:oracle-admits-closed-refusal-forms`)|All four refusal forms are admitted without oracle evidence.|
